<title>THAILAND: Thai Jan-Nov petroleum demand up 10.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Thai Jan-Nov petroleum demand up 10.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's petroleum demand in the first 11 months of 1996 rose by 10.1 percent to 884,470 barrels per day, the Petroleum Authority of Thailand (PTT) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Consumption of refined products rose 9.5 percent to average 772,100 bpd while demand for natural gas went up by 12.6 percent from the same period in 1995 to the equivalent of 162,370 bpd, PTT said in a statement.</p>
<p>Petroleum purchases in the first 11 months of 1996 averaged 1,067,130 bpd, a 22.9 percent increase from the same period.</p>
<p>Procurement from local sources rose 14.3 percent to 278,600 bpd, the report said.</p>
<p>The PTT detailed January-November petroleum use and procurement as follows:</p>
<p>			    Average bpd    Change from Jan-Nov 1995</p>
<p>			    (by product)</p>
<p>Total consumption</p>
<p> Gas oil		    306,040	   up 14.0 pct</p>
<p> Fuel oil		   168,710	   up  1.5 pct</p>
<p> Gasoline		   118,700	   up  9.6 pct</p>
<p> Aviation fuel	     58,060	   up  2.5 pct</p>
<p> Liquid petroleum gas    53,590	   up 18.1 pct</p>
<p> Kerosene		     1,710	   dn  2.3 pct</p>
<p> Natural Gas		162,370	   up 12.6 pct</p>
<p> Others			14,290		 N/A</p>
<p> TOTAL			884,470	   up 10.1 pct</p>
<p>Total Procurement</p>
<p> Imported crude oil     625,800	   up 41.3 pct</p>
<p> Gas Oil		     87,550	   dn 12.7 pct</p>
<p> Fuel Oil		    50,070	   dn 16.9 pct</p>
<p> Gasoline		     6,540	   dn 44.6 pct</p>
<p> Aviation Fuel		1,240	   dn 65.4 pct</p>
<p> Liquid petroleum gas     1,550	   up 318.9 pct</p>
<p> Bitumen			3,450	   up 40.2 pct</p>
<p> Lubricant		    2,330	   up 10.4 pct</p>
<p> TOTAL			778,530	   up 24.8 pct</p>
<p> Local sources	    278,600	   up 14.3 pct</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
